  "method": {
    "endpoint": "Parent wall clock around a fresh Node process through exit. node <entry> --video <master> --script <spoken> --transcript <asr> --out <local directory>. Includes file hashing, metadata, full decode, audio measurement, text comparison and report writes. Existing transcripts were reused; no new ASR.",
    "order": "One process at a time. Eight pairs per title, original first in four and optimized first in four. Title order alternated. File cache was not flushed. Traced stage runs and diagnostic candidate trials are separate and excluded from the whole distributions.",
    "reference": "Every complete real-video report deep-equaled the archived report except inspectedAt. The report fingerprint here replaces inputs with their byte counts and SHA-256 to omit local paths. Traced original and optimized frame CSV matched byte-for-byte after projecting the extra explicit PTS column out of the optimized scan.",
    "estimator": "Median of eight is the average of the fourth and fifth sorted values. Percent saved is 100*(1-optimizedMedian/originalMedian). Wall times are milliseconds.",
    "routing": "If the metadata read is clean, the first video is progressive H.264 yuv420p, 0 < pixels <= 2073600, nb_frames is a positive integer, and more than one CPU is available, fully decode with up to eight threads, frame threading and err_detect=explode. A warning or failed call, missing/estimated timestamps, wrong count, frame-time or end-time discrepancy switches to the original -show_frames call; its report determines the result. Other inputs keep the original scan."
  },
